Notes from meeting May 21, 2026 at 10:10 AM EDT

These notes have been sent to invited guests in your organization.

Open meeting notes

The content was auto-generated on May 21, 2026, 11:03 AM EDT and may  
contain errors.


Summary
Stakeholders aligned on construction logistics and safety measures for the  
upcoming sanctuary renovation and steeple project.


Project Timeline and Scope
Scaffolding construction begins July 6th with full site access by August  
3rd. Targeted scaffolding limits costs by avoiding full sanctuary coverage.

Site Logistics and Safety
Perimeter walls ensure safety while designated staging areas manage  
material transport. The team decided to use a color-coded photo map for  
stakeholder communication.

Operational Planning
Phase 2 roof work concludes August 28th following debris management and  
stained glass protection. Trusted partners are highlighted to demonstrate  
local project alignment.


Suggested next steps



[Cameron] Create Site Map: Create a visual site map using color-coded  
shapes to illustrate the locations of scaffolding, the crane, the dumpster,  
and the material staging path on site photos. Use blue lines for  
scaffolding, red for the crane, and green for the dumpster.

[Chris] Contact Scheduler: Contact Irma to obtain the church schedule for  
Sunday services and additional events. Use this calendar to coordinate the  
removal of protective plywood from stained glass windows to ensure  
functionality during service times.

[Cameron] Add Canister Photo: Include an example photograph of a storage  
canister within the final site visualization documents to clarify staging  
expectations.

[Cameron Reynolds] Include crane photo: Insert a picture of a truck crane  
with its arms extended into the project documentation.

[Chris Koelbl] Send vendor info: Text a list of project partners including  
Imperial Crane, Great Lakes Quickspace, Bone Supply, and Prime Scaffolding.  
Mention the business relationships these vendors share with the church  
congregation.

[Cameron Reynolds] Update documentation: Integrate the provided partner  
details into the project site map and presentation.

[Chris Koelbl] Submit project plan: Email the final site map and detailed  
project overview by the end of tomorrow.


We've updated the Decisions section based on your feedback.
What do you think?


